// A prefab: a piece of a place, drawn as rows of glyphs, and what each glyph
// stands for; see `../reward/treasure_room.ron` for the full field list.
//
// A landmark: the Watch Barracks' gatehouse, the first piece a floor of the
// barracks is grown round (`assets/pool.ron`, seeded `Span`, its stairs
// `Beyond`). A curtain wall of the old town's own pale stone laid across
// the middle of the floor, a tower at each end and the gatehouse at its
// heart, the gate passage three wide straight through it between two
// guardrooms, each lit by a brazier that throws its light out through the
// arches into the passage. A wall walk runs inside the curtain from tower
// to tower, and two posterns open on it, one in each face, far apart, so a
// floor has a second way through the wall for whoever walks it.
//
// The way in is drawn on one side of the wall and the way down on the
// other, so the gate is on the way, and remembered. Drawn lying along the
// map, and it may only be laid so: a half-turn and its mirrors, never on
// end, which a floor of the barracks is not tall enough to hold. The
// entries are the gate's two mouths and the two posterns; growth opens
// them by its own join, and an entry it never opens stays curtain wall.
(
    name: "The Gatehouse",
    ground: "hall floor",
    turn: Half,
    mirror: Both,
    rows: [
        "                                  #######EEE#######                                  ",
        "                                  #r....#ggg#r....#                                  ",
        "#########                         #......ggg......#                         #########",
        "#r......#                         #..t..#ggg#..t..#                         #.......#",
        "#.......############E##############.....#ggg#.....###########################.......#",
        "#...&...+.........................+.....#ggg#.....+.........................+...&...#",
        "#.......###########################.....#ggg#.....##############E############.......#",
        "#.......#                         #..&..#ggg#..&..#                         #......r#",
        "#########                         #......ggg......#                         #########",
        "                                  #....r#ggg#....r#                                  ",
        "                                  #######EEE#######                                  ",
    ],
    legend: {
        '#': Tile("curtain wall"),
        '.': Tile("hall floor"),
        'g': Tile("flagstones"),
        '+': Tile("door"),
        'r': Prop("rack"),
        't': Prop("table"),
        '&': Prop("brazier"),
        'E': Entry,
    },
)
